. * We would love to test the presence of the parents/children in the household
> , searched for the SOEP relevant variable and the only relevant (which we do 
> not have) was the bfkinhh – Member of Household. In this way we cannot contro
> l for the situation if the respondents live with their children in common hou
> sehold or not *
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * 
. 
. * As seen from the described variables, our model aims to test whether having
>  daughters is more likely associated with left-wing way of voting behaviour *
. * The analysis is moderated by the control variables and the general interest
>  in politics. *
. * The dependent variable is binary, meaning that the model aims to test wheth
> er the respondents with daughters are more likely to vote for the selected le
> ft-wing parties or not. *
. 
. 
. * Correct Specification would be Logit/Probit, but the extraction and exporti
> ng code is set up to export and local OLS results, which is a reason, why we 
> decided to stay with the OLS linear model * 
.         *logit party_closeness_dummy age sex2 education_years household_incom
